{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_gha_122",
      "name": "npm-dependency-cache",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Cache npm downloads without stale installs",
      "description": "Rice Rocket's test job spends 2.5 of its 4 minutes in `npm ci` downloading packages. The first cache a teammate added kept `api/node_modules` under a fixed key and skipped `npm ci` on a hit: the day `zod` joined the lockfile, CI restored the old `node_modules` and failed with `Cannot find module 'zod'`. The editor holds the test job with the `actions/cache` step and the install step missing, each marked by a `# [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that: npm's download cache (`~/.npm`) is kept between runs; a run with an unchanged `api/package-lock.json` restores it exactly and downloads nothing; a run after the lockfile changed restores the newest cache of the same OS and downloads only the changed packages; every run installs from the lockfile, so `node_modules` always matches it; a Windows runner never gets a Linux cache. Run grades the file with a simulator of actions/cache (immutable keys, restore-keys, branch scopes) over a series of CI runs.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "outcomes": [
        "fast-feedback"
      ],
      "points": 30,
      "hints": [
        "Follow one run after `zod` is added: what key does it compute, which saved entry does it find, what lands on disk, and does anything rebuild `node_modules` from the new lockfile?",
        "Look at the `path`, `key` and `restore-keys` inputs of `actions/cache`, at what `hashFiles()` returns when its pattern matches no file, and at what `npm ci` does to an existing `node_modules`.",
        "A Python job caching pip downloads uses `path: ~/.cache/pip`, `key: pip-${{ runner.os }}-${{ hashFiles('worker/requirements.txt') }}`, `restore-keys: |` followed by `pip-${{ runner.os }}-`, and always runs `pip install -r worker/requirements.txt` after the cache step."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "yaml",
        "filePath": ".github/workflows/ci.yml",
        "executionMode": "browser",
        "timeLimitMs": 2000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "First run misses and downloads everything; the next run with the same lockfile hits exactly",
          "input": {
            "checks": [
              "parse",
              "runs"
            ],
            "runs": [
              {
                "id": "first",
                "branch": "main",
                "os": "Linux",
                "lock": "3f9c1e"
              },
              {
                "id": "second",
                "branch": "main",
                "os": "Linux",
                "lock": "3f9c1e"
              }
            ]
          },
          "expected": {
            "parse": "ok",
            "runs": {
              "first": {
                "restore": "miss",
                "download": "all",
                "node_modules": "fresh"
              },
              "second": {
                "restore": "exact",
                "download": "none",
                "node_modules": "fresh"
              }
            }
          },
          "hidden": false,
          "score": 6
        },
        {
          "name": "After a lockfile change: partial restore, only new packages, fresh node_modules",
          "input": {
            "checks": [
              "runs"
            ],
            "runs": [
              {
                "id": "before",
                "branch": "main",
                "os": "Linux",
                "lock": "3f9c1e"
              },
              {
                "id": "zod-added",
                "branch": "main",
                "os": "Linux",
                "lock": "8b27d4"
              },
              {
                "id": "after",
                "branch": "main",
                "os": "Linux",
                "lock": "8b27d4"
              }
            ]
          },
          "expected": {
            "runs": {
              "before": {
                "restore": "miss",
                "download": "all",
                "node_modules": "fresh"
              },
              "zod-added": {
                "restore": "partial",
                "download": "changed packages",
                "node_modules": "fresh"
              },
              "after": {
                "restore": "exact",
                "download": "none",
                "node_modules": "fresh"
              }
            }
          },
          "hidden": false,
          "score": 6
        },
        {
          "name": "A feature branch restores the cache saved on main",
          "input": {
            "checks": [
              "runs"
            ],
            "runs": [
              {
                "id": "main",
                "branch": "main",
                "os": "Linux",
                "lock": "3f9c1e"
              },
              {
                "id": "feature",
                "branch": "feature/momo-pay",
                "os": "Linux",
                "lock": "3f9c1e"
              }
            ]
          },
          "expected": {
            "runs": {
              "main": {
                "restore": "miss",
                "download": "all",
                "node_modules": "fresh"
              },
              "feature": {
                "restore": "exact",
